{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfReykfebkHJhriKC3wdh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 06 is done and the loop is complete. Nothing remains to request.\n\n**What this iteration did.** It tested the two n ≤ 40 laws from items 03 and 04 against Chu & Stuckey's 200 corpus instances at 30–125. The ledger turned out to hold no node counts at all despite the brief, so the module refuted `optimum − 1` itself for the 140 instances at n ≥ 50 outside the two day-long classes, under both configurations. That took 5.65 core-hours, with 273 of 280 calls settled and 7 censored, and the counts are committed as `learning/data/ensemble/scale_nodes.csv`.\n\n**What holds to 125.** The refutation grows exponentially in n at fixed density in every class, with a power law three to five times worse. The mean optimum stays linear in n at fixed density. The density-2 class stays 2–6× harder than density 4 at every size, so customers per product, not optimum/n, is the ridge's size-stable coordinate. The pre-registered ridge law from §11 predicted 5 × 10¹¹ nodes at 125×125 density 2 and the two counts on record are 1.6 and 1.7 × 10¹¹, within a factor of 3 after eight decades of extrapolation.\n\n**What fails.** The campaign's growth rates overstate the corpus's by 0.005–0.018 per customer, which compounds to a factor of 6–34 at 125 for densities 6–10. The §12 formula's intercept and sparse slope are wrong, so its bias reaches +8 stacks at density 2 by 125 while staying within ±2 at densities 4–10. `tw_min_fill + 1` is +4.2 at 125. Every 90% conformal interval calibrated on n ≤ 40 fails at 50 or 75, so the plan's kill criterion is met for both quantities and §14 quotes no interval beyond n = 40. A side finding: Theorem 2's saving grows with n, to a median 37% at n = 100 and 83% on `Random-100-50-4`.\n\n**Bookkeeping.** §14 appended to `reports/ml_nature.md` with tables in `reports/scale_test_tables.md` and the figure in `reports/figures/scale_test.png`. Eight new tests; the full suite passes at 813. PROGRESS.md has the iteration entry, the count reads 6/6, the item is ticked, and `LOOP_COMPLETE` is the last line. Nothing was written to `solutions/`, no solver default changed, and nothing was committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":776,"cache_read_input_tokens":206946,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":776,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7437d77-4292-4a9d-949f-8cb6223ab1f3","uuid":"ed22886c-d789-46e0-8a6b-02860d807cbe","timestamp":"2026-09-26T07:28:00.045Z","request_id":"req_011CfReyixTgaRED3tbucqHk"}
